message: "If you use fleet-deploy in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "fleet-deploy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/fleet-deploy"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/fleet-deploy"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Rolling a change to a small heterogeneous fleet and proving it landed on each machine,
  for the case where a configuration management system is not an option: no agent to
  install, no inventory server, machines asleep half the day. One stdlib-only Python file
  enforcing one sentence: sent is not done and silence is not consent. A change counts as
  applied only when a command ran on that node and read back a fact; everything else is
  counted in a separate column out loud. Registration refuses parcels that cannot deliver
  their artifact, canary waves require a node of a different class before the fleet, a node
  may decline with a reason, and a node-down verdict expires after 30 days.
keywords:
  - deployment
  - fleet-management
  - canary-release
  - verification
  - devops
  - ai-agents
